mtPaint @VERSION@ - a painting program (GTK 3) for RISC OS

mtPaint 3.50.14 by Mark Tyler and Dmitry Groshev (GPL version 3), on GTK 3
through riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend: pixel art, photo retouching, palettes,
layers, animation frames. It reads and writes PNG, JPEG, GIF and BMP, and its own formats.

Using it
- Run it: mtPaint opens its window and puts its icon on the icon bar. Or
  drop a picture on !mtPaint in a Filer window.
- The icon bar icon: Select brings mtPaint's window to the front; Menu
  gives Info, Choices... (mtPaint's Preferences) and Quit.
- PNG, JPEG, GIF and BMP files double-clicked in the Filer while mtPaint
  is loaded, dropped on its icon, or saved to it from another program are
  loaded (it asks first if the picture has unsaved changes).
- Menu anywhere in mtPaint's windows (the picture, the toolbars, the
  palette) gives its menu.
- Small windows such as the Pan Window and the Pattern Chooser have a
  title bar and close icon; Escape also closes them.
- Mouse: Select paints with colour A; Adjust paints with colour B (the
  right button elsewhere), and Adjust on a tool button opens its
  settings.
- File > Save As: a Save box with mtPaint's options (format, compression)
  under it. Drag its file icon to a Filer window, or give a full name and
  click Save, or click Browse... for riscos-gtk's Save box or its
  directory browser. File > Open: drag a picture to the box from a Filer
  window, or click Browse...
- mtPaint's settings are kept in <Choices$Write>.mtPaint.

Messages
mtPaint's messages go to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.mtPaint.Log.

Needs
RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 or later machine (Raspberry Pi 2 or later, ARMX6,
Titanium...), SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, ARMEABISupport and Iconv
(PackMan). PThreadTicker is included.

